    note="two absences in the held record"
  >

  <p>
    Nothing in the held captures records an exchange freeze, a flagging
    commitment or any other custodial action against the four consolidation
    addresses as of 15 August 2026, and no captured source names an exchange or
    service that has undertaken to stop or mark deposits from them. The tracker
    record does show deposits attributed to the later wave-4 park reaching
    Bullish.com, Coinbase Prime Custody and KuCoin, and deposits attributed to
    the later Taproot wave reaching Binance, with no freeze or seizure of any
    of those reported either. That is an absence in what has been published and
    collected here, not a finding that no such step has been taken.
    <Claim
      basis="unverified"
      scope="Whether any exchange or custodial service has frozen or committed to flagging deposits from the attributed addresses"
      source="No captured source held by this project reports such a step as of 15 August 2026; the archive cannot observe unpublished compliance action"
      href="/record/changes/"
    />
  </p>

  <p>
